#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:5
#: 094d1215e9264c37b94b6ab934b2be91
msgid "NVidia TX1 as a Companion Computer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:7
#: 886c4313f32f4aaaa543d2ae7136f128
msgid "This page explains how to connect and configure an `NVidia TX1 <http://www.nvidia.com/object/jetson-tx1-dev-kit.html>`__ using `AuVidea.eu's J120 carrier board <http://auvidea.com/j120/>`__ so that it is able to communicate with a Pixhawk flight controller using the MAVLink protocol over a serial connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:10
#: d64c59b7a04c4dea8a3d61b19f3ec82a
msgid "Connecting the Pixhawk and TX1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:14
#: e9b45bcbdc4c4c48a08a7c4c9ab6fd71
msgid "Connect the Pixhawk's TELEM2 port to the J120's UART2 port's Ground, TX and RX pins as shown in the image above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:16
#: 76457de8d97147adb103bf724108745b
msgid "The Pixhawk and TX1 should be powered separately (the J120/TX1 through its 12V power input port, the Pixhawk through its POWER port).  They should be powered on at about the same time or the TX1 powered on first to avoid the Pixhawk interrupting the TX1's bootloader."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:19
#: 7d16844dae0b4d888237a656d5e16f7c
msgid "Setup the Pixhawk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:21
#: cb126831aa694b259ca307b56bbe14dd
msgid "Connect to the Pixhawk with a ground station (i.e. Mission Planner) and set the following parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:23
#: 526473b3c53e43269e7962d2409bf02c
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL <copter:SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 1 (the default) to enable MAVLink on the serial port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:24
#: 59d4e89d32ee48559bbfe81d87dbddc7
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_BAUD <copter:SERIAL2_BAUD>` = 921 so the Pixhawk can communicate with the TX1 at 921600 baud."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:25
#: 86bd459e4b514e9ca39c2c78a96983fc
msgid ":ref:`LOG_BACKEND_TYPE <copter:LOG_BACKEND_TYPE>` = 3 if you are using APSync to stream the dataflash log files to the TX1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:27
#: 8ff486830d23402881d6442398f44416
msgid "You may need to manually disable flow control on Telem2 although this is not normally required:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:29
#: fc817e87b41349e1b9a4806f1125195e
msgid ":ref:`BRD_SER2_RTSCTS <copter:BRD_SER2_RTSCTS>` = 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:31
#: 7021f3300a13487cb74d24778bd6cd31
msgid "As a side note the J120's UART2 appears on the TX1 as /dev/ttyTHS1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:34
#: fc45e8867a9449868f4c65f1c8e4ae56
msgid "Setup the TX1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:36
#: 694850fe0e714a4fb23445b22709f97a
msgid "There are two steps required to setting up the TX1:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:38
#: fde1374589c347aead26be15f1a27507
msgid "install JetPack-3.0 to an Ubuntu 16 desktop and flash the TX1 operating system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:39
#: 0af1ec7a558d4ab9983f635ab239cf62
msgid "flash the APSync image to the TX1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:42
#: b7aaa93f428a48bfa3988caaa5e4843c
msgid "Installing JetPack-3.0 and flashing the OS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:44
#: b33c2e9e2c8245dd855b23022d7fef30
msgid "First put the TX1 into bootloader mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:46
#: 0cf0a3d310bd4b0c9483d50bcbeb0ee4
msgid "connect the TX1 to an Ubuntu 16.04 machine using a USB cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:47
#: d7c383b19f8746a0851662d4f6730f0c
msgid "put the TX1 into bootloader mode by holding the \"Force Recovery\" button (aka \"REC\"), then press the \"Reset\" button (aka \"RST\") and then release the \"Force Recovery\" button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:48
#: f478eee12ffb40298d8477b613e5b5fd
msgid "check the TX1 is in bootloader mode by typing \"lsusb\" on the Ubuntu machine and look for \"NVidia Corp\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:52
#: f43420a05e6245658acec90eb739f796
msgid "Next install JetPack and flash the OS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:54
#: 3b9b370f5f9c4555b87d899e0d5f0b4a
msgid "connect an Ubuntu 16.04 machine to the internet and download `JetPack-3.1 <https://developer.nvidia.com/embedded/dlc/jetpack-l4t-3_1>`__ (nvidia login required)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:55
#: f3008618327a434dab8d186002815bd8
msgid "move the downloaded file to the directory you want JetPack installed into (i.e. \"~/Desktop/JetPack-3.1\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:56
#: fa5c2055e1a640a88bd81aacc549d967
msgid "make sure the file is executable by typing, \"chmod a+x JetPack-L4T-3.1-linux-x64.run\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:57
#: fd3b57ef441a45c58449370fec974fd6
msgid "start the installation by running the downloaded file, \"./JetPack-L4T-3.1-linux-x64.run\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:58
#: bd462aa8d1bc428fade17920f2b7d3d4
msgid "a \"JetPack L4T 3.1 Installer\" window should appear, press \"Next\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:59
#: 8995bd87a3f645848e084ee19363b005
msgid "a \"Installation Configuration\" page should appear confirming where JetPack will be installed, press \"Next\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:60
#: 35d1817fede0404db547fd0b2b863f35
msgid "a \"Select Development Environment\" page should appear allowing you to select the board type, select \"Jetson TX1\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:64
#: 9e6168ca97664534a3293668ffb90d74
msgid "an \"Installing\" page will appear asking for your password in order to begin the local installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:65
#: 4d50bdc7fe9644d399549dc5f811ab31
msgid "a \"JetPack L4T Component Manager\" screen should appear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:67
#: fc3b0938a01b47bc8aed64762fa07586
msgid "from the top left, select \"JetPack L4T 3.0\" (this may need to be selected twice to work)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:68
#: f8f2b02895fd4e0fb9c29d967bc81c36
msgid "for \"Host - Ubuntu\" set the \"Action\" column to \"no action\" for everything (select \"Keep & Apply\" if a question pops up)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:69
#: 48eb1159e76d4a0c8e58e17b6e003cdc
msgid "Target - Jetson TX1: mixed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:70
#: 47cee8c3a877444f814624b44232e36d
msgid "Linux for Tegra Host Side Image Setup: install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:71
#: 59c5e7dcb2a048e797770a8b25b0957f
msgid "Flash OS Image to Target: install 24.2.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:72
#: 46cb6b4c5d2f45b495496896002bc987
msgid "Install on Target: mixed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:73
#: 0bfdb06438574d34967c81654b476b12
msgid "CUDA Toolkit: install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:74
#: b307d0ed2a5d4e3f9f2922b1a58e95da
msgid "Compile CUDA Samples: no action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:75
#: 6bccc729ad3d430fa214808fac6f1316
msgid "PerfKit: install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:76
#: 4a44d6b22c5e470ca34ecd70394c2641
msgid "TensorRT: install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:77
#: 425c94d6a41d48cdb064676eccb04d17
msgid "Multimedia API package: no action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:78
#: a3d4eedcb8b84146b51b76b935be5f09
msgid "cuDNN Package: install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:79
#: f24ab1eceeeb449d834187052aca7d00
msgid "OpenCV for Tegra: install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:80
#: 4aec3893a52f47bcb342863b8836f34e
msgid "VisionWorks on TX1 Target: no action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:84
#: b74bd4674ed2462b91827482f00a4640
msgid "an \"Terms & Conditions\" window may appear, select \"Accept All\" and push the \"Accept\" button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:85
#: 55fa15b8771b46f996b1703e64fda388
msgid "a \"Host installation is complete\" window should appear, press \"Next\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:86
#: 1d804b9b3029445bb680b4d78c888822
msgid "a \"Network Layout - Jetson TX1\" window should appear, select \"Device accesses Internet via router/switch\" after first ensuring the TX1 and Ubuntu machine are connected to the internet with an ethernet cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:87
#: cd3a8c504f0a41afba3f149669d837eb
msgid "if a \"Network Interface Selection\" window pops up, select the Ubuntu machine's network connection that corresponds to the ethernet cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:91
#: 1dd47444f7a04ac8a206756ce8ad4c89
msgid "a \"Post Installation Jetson TX1\" window may appear, press \"Next\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:92
#: 451342e4a6cb4a1abc08d212deff251f
msgid "a black console window titled, \"Post Installation\" should appear asking that the TX1 be put in bootloader mode (this should already have been done), Press \"Enter\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:93
#: efbb55fe6e1c45e48bbad433843cc6bc
msgid "installation should continue for about 15min and finally a message should appear asking you to close the black console window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:94
#: 3e32d5329d6c4614bf7cb6f7984042b1
msgid "an \"Installation Complete\" window should appear, leave \"Remove downloaded files\" unchecked and press \"Finish\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:96
#: 6eafd2b0c374468aa83aceeacb309a15
msgid "These instructions can also be found in `\"Step1 : install NVidia image onto the TX1\" from here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/companion/blob/master/Nvidia_JTX1/Ubuntu/1_create_base_image.txt>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:99
#: 042e57438254463c8d37461f52010e40
msgid "Flashing the APSync image to the TX1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:101
#: d1598214ce534250b66c5cbe1a8a7cb9
msgid "connect a USB cable from the Ubuntu 16 machine to the TX1 development board, power on the TX1 and put the TX1 into bootloader mode (see instructions above)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:102
#: df79646ff2ed49629ced194880210e46
msgid "On the Ubuntu 16 machine, download the latest `APSync image for the tx1 <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Companion/apsync/apsync-tx1-latest-img.xz>`__ from `firmware.ardupilot.org <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Companion/apsync/>`__ (look for images starting with \"tx1\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:103
#: 2e91416ca71f4c56aa5c79700465672d
msgid "uncompress the downloaded image (i.e. open a file explorer, right-mouse-button click on the file and select \"Extract Here\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:104
#: 171c990ce25c414aadc6c6ab1865071d
msgid "on the Ubuntu machine, from the directory where you installed JetPack (i.e. ~/Desktop/JetPack-3.1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:105
#: 60bfa61a24f6427b99a5331fb2cd6cea
msgid "cd 64_TX1/Linux_for_Tegra_64_tx1/bootloader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:106
#: 4dce2ed3d97140929736497cdfa63ecd
msgid "run this command but replace IMAGE.img with the name of the image downloaded, sudo ./tegraflash.py --bl cboot.bin --applet nvtboot_recovery.bin --chip 0x21 --cmd \"write APP IMAGE.img\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:110
#: 5feed4d37afb4b43ad4edbdebbc7ec35
msgid "Official instructions from NVidia on flashing images can be found `here <https://devtalk.nvidia.com/default/topic/898999/jetson-tx1/tx1-r23-1-new-flash-structure-how-to-clone-/post/4784149/#4784149>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:113
#: 1544ce8971144f60a3c9b60b5a558a9a
msgid "Notes if using ZED camera"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:115
#: 2ae48eb19ae64d299c16c57507510d53
msgid "If you are using the `StereoLabs <https://www.stereolabs.com/>`__ :ref:`ZED camera <copter:common-zed>` then the TX1 will need to be powered up once with the ethernet cable plugged in so that it has access to the internet in order to download the camera's factory calibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.rst:117
#: 864e70554bef49e5b9e2f35010a6fdd3
msgid "If using the AUVidea J120 board, the ZED camera may need to be plugged into the lower USB port to work correctly."
msgstr ""
